YA(2nd)AP - fated the priest on NAO

It's been nearly a year and a half since my first ascension.  Since
then I've lost a valk and a priest on the astral plane, both
heartbreaking.

Began as fated-Pri-Hum-Mal-Cha with a spellbook of identify, not very
useful until he gained some levels.  However, this priest's first 
goal was to go through sokoban and back to mine town without gaining a 
level.  The protection racket attempt was made easier by taming
several puppies and kittens with food (or tripe...or corpses...).
He had to kill a couple things in sokoban that got between the rock
and the hole, and completed it with a bag of holding and level 2.

In minetown, he found 2 magic lamps.  One became a GDSM, and the
second became emercency wish/permanent light.  Praying too often
pissed off Loki, who dropped fated's level back to 1, and then
donating sokoban's loot and profits from dungeon booty gave a
natural AC of 1.  

Much later, we went to the castle for the wand.  Pet gremlins
everywhere kept most beasts off his back, while stronger pets killed
lots of stuff.  Wand identified 0:1, so fated got some charging
scrolls, typo-induced cram ration (oops), and FrostBrand. The other
wishes were saved for future needs.

Time spent identifing, learning, and mapping found nearly everything
else needed.  The only gaping holes were teleportitis without
control and lack of free action.  Reverse-genoing tengus in sokoban
helped the one, but the other was to be a danger for some time (the
wand was gone by this point).  Ludios didn't help a whole lot, so
instead fated completed the quest, goofed about some more, and
eventually marked the vibrating square with the bell, candelabram,
and some boulders.

Back at base camp, fated polymorphed some rings to get free action
(finally!), and himself to eat some rings of protection.  I think
naked AC was -3 or -4.  Only after this did fun really begin.

All monies had been donated to priests, and rather than kill them
(and risk angry gods), fated stole all Izchak's candles.  Chaotics
have all the fun.  Putting the candles on the candelabram, fated
realized there were only 6.  The journey to Rodney didn't find any,
either.  However, fated's second blunder vaporized FrostBrand when
he (now a she) was intending to improve daggars.  Curse you,
Impatience!  A nearby titan heard the fuming, and his summoned
minions gave fated a run for her money.

Rodney was also no picknick - the wizard kept dodging death rays and
nearly ended the quest in his own right.

With book, bell, and candelabram in hand, the magic lamp was used
for that emergency wish (7 more candles, if you please).  Rodney
double-troubled in the sanctum, but in an unusual show of mercy, the
RND had both rodneys and the high-priest line up.  Death ray, and
all three went down.  Score!

Fled to the plains, where fated learned that confused spells of
detect treasure don't work like confused scrolls of detect gold.
That's planning for you.  Conflicting and levetating eventually saw
the way to Astral.  Alter the Right, behind Pestilence, was odin's.
A monster wielding Vorpal Blade made fated's heart beat faster, and
Death dropped max health from 130s to 86.  But then Vorpy cleared a
path, and Alter the Center was Loki's.  Hurrah!


